  "reason": "With no completed experiments, there is zero evidence about any design axis (modality, encoder, profile strategy, aggregation, fusion). The most informative first step is to establish a minimal, well-understood baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) uses the simplest standard RNA representation (PCA, 2000 components), avoids confounding from multi-profile aggregation or fusion choices, and is computationally lightweight. It anchors the RNA performance floor against which every subsequent experiment—image-only, multimodal, alternative encoders, multiprofile—can be compared. Establishing this floor first lets the next experiments directly test whether adding images, switching encoders, or using multimodal fusion provides a meaningful gain, making each follow-up experiment maximally interpretable under the limited budget."
}

